# 39. SECURITY RULES

Never weaken backend authorization to solve a frontend UX issue.

Never:

- trust role strings from UI input
- trust client-side permission results as authority
- trust client-side signature permission
- expose server file paths
- expose SQL errors
- expose JWTs
- expose refresh tokens
- expose passwords
- expose password hashes
- copy seeded credentials into documentation or responses
- allow arbitrary history insertion
- bypass workflow assignments
- bypass current-step validation

Authorization must remain resource-specific and server-enforced.

