# 42. VERIFY BEFORE CHANGING DATABASE CODE

Before schema work inspect:

- current DocuTracker table definitions in `backend/scripts/init-schema.sql`
- all relevant DocuTracker migrations in `backend/scripts/migrations/docutracker/`
- backend queries
- Dart models
- API response mapping
- tests
- migration rollup configuration and the existing generator (read-only unless separately approved)

**Follow the mandatory workflow in Section 29:** create a forward DocuTracker migration, synchronize the authorized DocuTracker sections of `init-schema.sql`, update the rollup if required, and verify fresh-init versus upgrade parity. Do not modify other modules' schema or run a migration against the shared/live DB without approval.

Pay special attention to existing migration/init-schema drift.

Never invent a table or column because a feature "probably needs it."

